Trace the vendor clock register write that precedes the HC mode switch

The eMMC boot stops right after the "GCC sdcc1_apps not mapped" line, so it
is not yet known whether the hang is in the CORE_VENDOR_SPEC read or in the
following write. Print the value about to be written to separate the two.

--- a/bsd/dev/tulip_sdhci.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/tulip_sdhci.c
@@ -2190,0 +2191 @@
+        printf("TULIP SDHCI: writing VENDOR_SPEC 0x%08x\n", CORE_VENDOR_SPEC_BOARD_VAL);
